  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The constituents of nucleic acids are nitrogenous bases, sugar and phosphoric acid. The sugar present in DNA is D(-)-2-deoxyribose  and the sugar present in RNA is D(-) ribose. Due to these D(-)-sugar components, DNA and RNA molecules are chiral molecules.<br/><br/> <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/znnjgwadmeoeljdzcmdvovakstrjcfdtanmsffiyhzkejsghon.jpeg\"/>",
